WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.334
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.400
You're here!

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.267
Happy you're here.
I love you.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.667
Guys, Halloween is right
around the corner.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.434
I'm excited about this,
but listen to this.

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:15.167
A new report found that a bunch
of chocolate products

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:20.100
contain a concerning amount of
lead and other heavy metals.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.067
In response, Hershey's put out
a statement that said,

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.534
"You're supposed to take
the tin foil off, you morons."

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.267
Unwrap it.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.634
Of course, everyone's decorating
their houses for Halloween,

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.267
and this year it seems like a
lot of people had the same idea.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.100
Watch this.
-Taylor Swift mania

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.100
is taking over Halloween.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.934
-One Wisconsin woman
put this Eras Tour-themed

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.767
decor up in her front yard.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.000
-Swifties are sure
to be enchanted

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.567
by this haunting sight.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.601
-A certain skeletal
football player

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.734
in awe of an uncanny pop star.
-In Indiana,

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.601
Swift-themed
Halloween decorations.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:57.267
-All the decorations
are Taylor Swift.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.267
-This is Taylor Swift-kin,

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:03.434
a nearly 400-pound pumpkin
dedicated to Taylor Swift.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.234
-Taylor was like,
"Thank you for all the tributes

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.801
and that one horrendous insult."

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.834
Yikes.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.200
Yep, Halloween is almost here,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.701
which means there are
pumpkin products everywhere.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:16.834
Starbucks, Oreos, Wendy's, Ihop.
Everyone's getting in on it.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.767
And maybe nowhere
more than Trader Joe's.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.067
They go nuts for pumpkin.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.934
In fact, check out this ad
I just saw.

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.000
-Hey, pumpkin lovers,
Trader Joe's

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.801
is your one-stop-shop
for pumpkin this fall.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:30.400
Our fan-favorite
pumpkin bread mix is back!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.534
Plus we've got pumpkin scones,
pumpkin bagels,

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.934
pumpkin brioche toast,
pumpkin cheesecake,

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:38.367
pumpkin yogurt,
and even pumpkin soap.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.367
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.267
Throw it all
in your pumpkin cart

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.667
and pay at our pumpkin register
with our pumpkin employees

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:48.267
to feed your pumpkin wife and
pumpkin kids and pumpkin dog.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:49.534
[ Dog barks ]

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.501
Don't forget to bring
your tote bag!

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:54.133
Trader Joe's --
we've got pumpkins!

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.467
-Oh! [ Chuckles ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:58.033
That's nice.
It's a little scary, right?

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.868
Well, switching gears
to some political news,

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.133
the House finally
elected a speaker.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.467
His name is Mike Johnson,

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.467
and most people
don't really know who he is.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:12.434
So if you're not familiar,
here's a picture of him.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.467
I'm sorry.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.901
That -- That's not Mike Johnson.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.634
That's Mike Flood.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.934
He's also a congressman,
but he's not the new speaker.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.300
This is Mike Johnson.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.334
Wait, no, sorry.
That's -- That's Mike Turner.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.133
That's Mike Turner.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.300
That's Mike Carey.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.167
That's Mike Kelly.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.868
That's Mike Gallagher.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.968
That's Mike Pence.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.267
That's Mike Tyson.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.167
That's Mike Myers.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.467
That's also Mike Myers.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:37.567
Mike Myers.

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:38.701
Mike Myers.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:40.300
Mike Myers.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.200
Michael Myers.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.767
That's Mike Wazowski.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:47.467
Oh, come on! The speaker's
name is Mike Johnson!

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.801
-Yeah.
-No. That's Magic...Johnson.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.534
That's Magic Mike.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.601
That's Randy Johnson.

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:57.567
That's
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:01.234
That's a bad wax statue
of Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:03.667
That's a bottle
of Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.434
Scarlett Johansson.

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:07.567
That's Lil Jon-son.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.234
Why is this so hard?
He's our speaker of the House.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:13.300
We should know who he is.
His name is Mike Johnson!

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.367
No, that's Mick Jagger!
His name is Mike Johnson!

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:20.167
Will someone please just get the
right picture of Mike Johnson?

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.734
There we go. Thank you.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.901
Was that so hard?

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.100
Meanwhile, earlier today,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.901
Mike Johnson met
with President Biden

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.133
for the first time
since becoming speaker.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:37.100
Johnson is pretty famous
for being an election denier,

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.968
so it got pretty awkward
when he said,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:42.334
"Good to meet you,
'President' Biden."

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.934
But the meeting
was very friendly.

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:45.901
Biden even invited Johnson
to pet his dog.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:49.634
[ Laughter ]
And this was nice.

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.801
Biden told a story
about his days in Congress,

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.067
and by the time it was over,

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.901
Johnson was already
voted out as speaker.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.300
Did you guys see this
today in Phoenix?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.167
Uber started offering
driverless rides.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:05.367
Even worse, the driver
is still there just to chat.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.133
Lyft also has a version
of driverless rides,

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.067
but they just put a cinder
block on the gas pedal.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.033
Some more business news.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.667
I saw that Domino's
is giving away

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:22.367
$1 million worth of free pizzas

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.534
to customers
with student loan payments.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:29.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.667
Customers are like, "Okay,

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:33.467
but what if you gave us
$1 million worth of dollars?"

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:36.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.300
Guys, Britney Spears's
new memoir is out,

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.634
and people were surprised
to hear

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:45.801
that she has Michelle Williams
to do the audio book.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.567
I'm not sure why
everyone's so surprised.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.601
Celebrities reading
other celebrities' audio books

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.000
is actually pretty common.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.734
I mean, for example,
John Travolta

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.400
narrated Prince Harry's
book "Spare."

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.434
-Did he really?
-Yeah.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.801
-[ As Travolta ]
Upon arriving home,

00:04:56.801 --> 00:04:58.300
I'd been horrified
to discover

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.734
that my nether regions
was frost-nipped as well,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.334
and while the ears
and the cheeks

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.801
were already healing,
the todger wasn't."

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:07.200
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.934
[ Applause ]

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.267
-I mean...
-I didn't know that.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:16.534
-Yeah. Jerry Seinfeld narrated
Elton John's book, "Me."

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.534
-[ As Seinfeld ]
I've played pianos,

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:22.167
I've jumped on pianos,
I've fallen off pianos,

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:25.167
I've pushed a piano
into the crowd!"

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You didn't know that?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.067
Yeah.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.801
Adam Sandler narrated
Matthew McConaughey's book

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.767
"Greenlights."
-[ As Sandler ] There is nothing

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.167
wrong with smoking
a little fun stuff

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:41.467
and playing your drums naked
at night in your own home;

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:44.567
who do they think they are
comin' in your house like that?!

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:46.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I mean, these are --

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:50.234
these are great audio books.
-Oh. On Audible.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:53.601
-Barry -- Barry Gibb narrated
Stanley Tucci's book "Taste."

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.934
-[ As Gibb ] To me,
eating well is not just about

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:59.767
what tastes good
but about the connections

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.000
that are made through
the food itself.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.434
-Yeah, it's a great --
It's fantastic. Listen.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.167
And finally,
this might surprise you,

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.434
but Al Pacino did
the narration for my book,

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.133
"Your Baby's First Word
Will Be Dada."

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:14.334
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:15.601
-[ As Pacino ] Dada!

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.234
Moo!

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:18.868
Dada!

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.033
Baa!

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:21.667
Dada!

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:22.701
Quack!

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.200
Dada!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.634
Hoooah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.400
-It's just -- It's fun. Anyways,
the holidays are coming up.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.167
[ Chuckles ]
-Wow!

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:33.167
Wow.

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:35.501
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:36.701
-Guys, get this.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:39.601
Mattel just reported
a massive jump in sales

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.367
thanks to the Barbie movie.
Yeah.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:44.300
Unfortunately, Hasbro's sales
of "Oppenheimer" toys

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.501
have been really disappointing.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.133
[ Laughter ]
Hey, guys, I read that

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:53.767
Beyoncé just launched
a new perfume called Cé Noir.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.834
It's pretty cool.
Well, it turns out Cé Noir

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.834
isn't the only new fragrance
on the market.

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.334
A lot of people, even companies,

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:01.901
have released new fragrances
in time for the holidays.

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:03.067
I'll show you what I mean.
For instance,

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.601
President Biden
has a new cologne.

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:05.701
It's called...

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.434
[whispering] Malarkáy.

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:12.100
That's right.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.767
The NFL also launched
their own fragrance...

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.133
[whispering] Obsession...

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:18.400
With Taylor Swift.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:23.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:26.734
Similarly, Ticketmaster
just released a new fragrance...

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:28.434
[whispering] Bleu It.

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:31.634
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.467
New speaker of the House
Mike Johnson

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:35.300
even released his own cologne...

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.300
[whispering] Choice No. 5.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:41.167
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:44.567
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert
just released her new perfume...

00:07:44.567 --> 00:07:46.334
[whispering] Beetle J'uice.

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:50.400
And now Congressman
George Santos

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.968
has launched a new fragrance...

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:53.601
[whispering] L'Bullsheé.

00:07:53.601 --> 00:07:57.534
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:57.534 --> 00:08:00.534
And finally, Donald Trump
just released his new scent...

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:02.200
[whispering] Golden Toilette.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:05.901
Well, good luck to all of them
this holiday season.

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:07.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:07.734 --> 00:08:10.934
Well...

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.901
finally, I heard about a man
in New York City

00:08:12.901 --> 00:08:15.000
who was freed after
being locked overnight

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.100
in the safe room
of a jewelry store.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.467
The guy was like,
"Hey, I'm not going to sue.

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:20.834
And with that being said,
please don't check

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:21.968
my stool tomorrow morning."

